    {
      "id": "5tmbV1a3MiPj_5e0lesj9",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2293.3555051204235,
      "y": 7606.214986052521,
      "width": 2601.97119140625,
      "height": 45,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b7Q",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 237473502,
      "version": 69,
      "versionNonce": 766132574,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1783084698046,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "- Each time one of the user you follow,  posts, the fan-out worker looks up their followers (not their own row) and writes into each follower's row:",
      "fontSize": 36,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "- Each time one of the user you follow,  posts, the fan-out worker looks up their followers (not their own row) and writes into each follower's row:",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "wDrOqVajOSwrH02oYIh7y",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2314.416620318242,
      "y": 7674.752241594917,
      "width": 1650.923583984375,
      "height": 360,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b7R",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1697096286,
      "version": 61,
      "versionNonce": 994516226,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1783084833440,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Storage:\nconst POST_ID_BYTES = 10; \nconst MAX_FEED_SIZE = 200;\nconst BYTES_PER_USER = POST_ID_BYTES * MAX_FEED_SIZE; // 2,000 bytes = ~2KB\n\nconst TOTAL_USERS = 2_000_000_000;\nconst TOTAL_STORAGE_BYTES = BYTES_PER_USER * TOTAL_USERS;\n// = 4,000,000,000,000 bytes = ~4TB",
      "fontSize": 36,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Storage:\nconst POST_ID_BYTES = 10; \nconst MAX_FEED_SIZE = 200;\nconst BYTES_PER_USER = POST_ID_BYTES * MAX_FEED_SIZE; // 2,000 bytes = ~2KB\n\nconst TOTAL_USERS = 2_000_000_000;\nconst TOTAL_STORAGE_BYTES = BYTES_PER_USER * TOTAL_USERS;\n// = 4,000,000,000,000 bytes = ~4TB",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "7GS-TlmwTz_bRAVu8K2Sq",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2280.1964820518765,
      "y": 8213.848262641184,
      "width": 1060.41552734375,
      "height": 45,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b7S",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1720324738,
      "version": 19,
      "versionNonce": 1587250434,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1783085086869,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "2) How do we handle users with a large number of followers?",
      "fontSize": 36,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "2) How do we handle users with a large number of followers?",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "3rx9Im4Dw_h7MmfhHTt3d",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2348.279368243432,
      "y": 8272.128200081697,
      "width": 1799.531494140625,
      "height": 90,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b7T",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 911394078,
      "version": 6,
      "versionNonce": 1509112194,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1783090035047,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "-  when a user with a lot of followers creates a post, we need to write to millions of feeds efficiently\n",
      "fontSize": 36,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "-  when a user with a lot of followers creates a post, we need to write to millions of feeds efficiently\n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "WayF53be5nqX45u23c5JM",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2368.629811513894,
      "y": 8340.85806068927,
      "width": 1394.3514404296875,
      "height": 315,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b7U",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 763678914,
      "version": 58,
      "versionNonce": 144523778,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1783090594403,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "1. Client → API Gateway → Post Service\n2. Post Service writes the post to the Posts table (direct, synchronous)\n3. Post Service pushes a message onto Post Create Queue (async, decoupled)\n4. Post Service returns to the client immediately — doesn't wait for fan-out\n                    ↓\n5. Feed Workers (a separate pool) pull messages off Post Create Queue\n6. Feed Workers do the fan-out: look up followers, write into PrecomputedFeed",
      "fontSize": 36,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "1. Client → API Gateway → Post Service\n2. Post Service writes the post to the Posts table (direct, synchronous)\n3. Post Service pushes a message onto Post Create Queue (async, decoupled)\n4. Post Service returns to the client immediately — doesn't wait for fan-out\n                    ↓\n5. Feed Workers (a separate pool) pull messages off Post Create Queue\n6. Feed Workers do the fan-out: look up followers, write into PrecomputedFeed",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "ZsN-y8EqfoR18A5EYLRv2",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2352.949340429618,
      "y": 8703.053437154393,
      "width": 3112.126708984375,
      "height": 1755,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b7V",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 489030622,
      "version": 357,
      "versionNonce": 501491614,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1783091899779,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Fan-out-on-write means: when someone posts, write their postId into every follower's PrecomputedFeed row. \n\nThat's fine for a normal user with 300 followers — 300 writes. But Justin Bieber has 90 million followers. \nOne tweet = 90 million writes, all triggered by a single createPost call. That's the \"hot write\" problem — the mirror image of the hot read problem the Post cache solved.\nThe key insight: don't treat every account the same\nNot every account needs to be precomputed. The approach flags certain follow relationships as \"don't bother precomputing this one\":\n\ninterface FollowItem {\n  followerId: string;\n  followeeId: string;\n  createdAt: number;\n  isPrecomputed: boolean;  // false = this relationship is skipped during fan-out\n}\n\nisPrecomputed: false gets set on all follow rows pointing at Bieber — every one of his 90M followers has a row saying \"don't push posts from Bieber into my precomputed feed.\"\nWrite side: the async worker simply skips these\n\nWhen Bieber posts, this function does almost nothing — no queue backlog, no 90M writes, no cost. The problem is solved not by making the write faster, \nbut by not doing the write at all for this account.\n\nRead side: this is where the \"cost\" of skipping shows up\nIf we never wrote Bieber's posts into anyone's precomputed feed, those posts have to come from somewhere when a follower opens their feed. \nThis is where fan-out-on-read comes back in, but now scoped to just the handful of celebrity accounts a user follows (not their entire follow list):\n\nasync function getFeed(userId: string, pageSize: number): Promise<FeedResponse> {\n  // Path A: precomputed feed (fast) — this has everything EXCEPT Bieber's posts\n  const precomputedIds = await getPrecomputedFeedIds(userId);\n  const precomputedPosts = await batchGetPosts(precomputedIds.slice(0, pageSize));\n\n  // Path B: live query for the few celebrities this user follows\n  const celebrityAuthorIds = await getNonPrecomputedFollowees(userId); // usually a short list\n  const celebrityPosts = await getRecentPostsForAuthors(celebrityAuthorIds, pageSize);\n\n  // Merge both sorted-by-time lists into one feed\n  const merged = mergeByTimestampDesc(precomputedPosts, celebrityPosts).slice(0, pageSize);\n\n  return { items: merged, nextCursor: /* ... */ };\n}\n",
      "fontSize": 36,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Fan-out-on-write means: when someone posts, write their postId into every follower's PrecomputedFeed row. \n\nThat's fine for a normal user with 300 followers — 300 writes. But Justin Bieber has 90 million followers. \nOne tweet = 90 million writes, all triggered by a single createPost call. That's the \"hot write\" problem — the mirror image of the hot read problem the Post cache solved.\nThe key insight: don't treat every account the same\nNot every account needs to be precomputed. The approach flags certain follow relationships as \"don't bother precomputing this one\":\n\ninterface FollowItem {\n  followerId: string;\n  followeeId: string;\n  createdAt: number;\n  isPrecomputed: boolean;  // false = this relationship is skipped during fan-out\n}\n\nisPrecomputed: false gets set on all follow rows pointing at Bieber — every one of his 90M followers has a row saying \"don't push posts from Bieber into my precomputed feed.\"\nWrite side: the async worker simply skips these\n\nWhen Bieber posts, this function does almost nothing — no queue backlog, no 90M writes, no cost. The problem is solved not by making the write faster, \nbut by not doing the write at all for this account.\n\nRead side: this is where the \"cost\" of skipping shows up\nIf we never wrote Bieber's posts into anyone's precomputed feed, those posts have to come from somewhere when a follower opens their feed. \nThis is where fan-out-on-read comes back in, but now scoped to just the handful of celebrity accounts a user follows (not their entire follow list):\n\nasync function getFeed(userId: string, pageSize: number): Promise<FeedResponse> {\n  // Path A: precomputed feed (fast) — this has everything EXCEPT Bieber's posts\n  const precomputedIds = await getPrecomputedFeedIds(userId);\n  const precomputedPosts = await batchGetPosts(precomputedIds.slice(0, pageSize));\n\n  // Path B: live query for the few celebrities this user follows\n  const celebrityAuthorIds = await getNonPrecomputedFollowees(userId); // usually a short list\n  const celebrityPosts = await getRecentPostsForAuthors(celebrityAuthorIds, pageSize);\n\n  // Merge both sorted-by-time lists into one feed\n  const merged = mergeByTimestampDesc(precomputedPosts, celebrityPosts).slice(0, pageSize);\n\n  return { items: merged, nextCursor: /* ... */ };\n}\n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
